        /// <item><description><see cref="CSDL.Props.WindowSdrWhiteLevelFloat">WindowSdrWhiteLevelFloat</see>: the value of SDR white in the <see cref="CSDL.Video.Colorspace.SRGBLinear">SRGBLinear</see> colorspace. On Windows this corresponds to the SDR white level in scRGB colorspace, and on Apple platforms this is always 1.0 for EDR content. This property can change dynamically when <see cref="CSDL.EventType.WindowHDRStateChanged">WindowHDRStateChanged</see> is sent.</description></item>
        /// <item><description><see cref="CSDL.Props.WindowHDRHeadroomFloat">WindowHDRHeadroomFloat</see>: the additional high dynamic range that can be displayed, in terms of the SDR white point. When HDR is not enabled, this will be 1.0. This property can change dynamically when <see cref="CSDL.EventType.WindowHDRStateChanged">WindowHDRStateChanged</see> is sent.</description></item>
        /// </list>
        /// <para>On Android:</para>
        /// <list type="bullet">
        /// <item><description><see cref="CSDL.Props.WindowAndroidWindowPointer">WindowAndroidWindowPointer</see>: the ANativeWindow associated with the window</description></item>
        /// <item><description><see cref="CSDL.Props.WindowAndroidSurfacePointer">WindowAndroidSurfacePointer</see>: the EGLSurface associated with the window</description></item>
        /// </list>
